Uncertainty, sensitivity and optimization of the whole service (@wu-system-uncertainty: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #source "../sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS", #source "../sources/WaterTAP-Process-Models.lingua#r_6JCG0EJT4DZTWJTNKZQXF1Y3JD", #source "../sources/Benchmark-Simulation-Model-2-IWA.lingua#r_7S4V5ZYP2VFKZ6VHSBS4Z2G5BF", #water-and-sanitation "Read-primary-water-research-and-check-what-can-be-reproduced.lingua#r_2C4RCEREJVM4WKR7CKR6VE7HZF") { r_1NHGPKNEXKPQE1C5YT5AS86BH6
**Read:** [Assessment of Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data — von Sperling, Verbyla and Oliveira](../sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS), the uncertainty and modelling foundations already linked, and the complete methods underlying your selected advanced study. Use [WaterTAP — inspectable water-treatment models](../sources/WaterTAP-Process-Models.lingua#r_6JCG0EJT4DZTWJTNKZQXF1Y3JD) and [Benchmark Simulation Model no. 2 — IWA technical description](../sources/Benchmark-Simulation-Model-2-IWA.lingua#r_7S4V5ZYP2VFKZ6VHSBS4Z2G5BF) to compare optimization or performance evaluation under explicit assumptions.

Measurement error, uncertain parameters, unknown future demand and an incomplete process model are different sources of uncertainty. Sensitivity asks how an output responds to a change; identifiability asks whether observations can distinguish parameters; optimization searches within a specified model and feasible region. None establishes that omitted constraints are satisfied.

**Work:** Begin with one-at-a-time changes that can be interpreted physically, then examine important interactions and correlated inputs. Check numerical convergence separately. Define quality, capacity, resource and receiving-route constraints before comparing objectives. Show where an attractive optimum is close to a poorly known feasibility boundary.

Compare expected performance with adverse but credible conditions and a decision that can be revised as evidence arrives. In an advanced study, justify probability distributions or use explicit bounded scenarios when probabilities lack evidence. Report multiple objectives where a single weighted score would conceal who receives the benefit and who bears the loss. Explain the decision in plain language as well as equations.

**Return:** [Water, sanitation and industrial utilities](../Water-sanitation-and-industrial-utilities.lingua#r_7B9GRCJFHVBEEQEXKWCR2QMMPN).
